adjudication.rationale:
In `packages/emails/email-manager.ts`, `sendAddGuestsEmails` maps over `calendarEvent.attendees` and for attendees whose email is in `newGuests` it sends `new AttendeeScheduledEmail(...)` instead of the newly added `AttendeeAddGuestsEmail` (which uses `new_guests_added` / `guests_added_event_type_subject`). This is directly shown by:
```ts
if (newGuests.includes(attendee.email)) {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeScheduledEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
} else {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeAddGuestsEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
}
```
So newly added guests will receive the normal “scheduled/confirmed” email content rather than the new “guests added” email content/templates referenced in the finding.
